No — everyone in the crew stayed within the rules.

Our information came only from:
- announced positions on the scroll;
- shared dig readings, including the fact that a shared dig meant that square was not the cave;
- turn numbers printed on scroll messages;
- the blocked-direction reports given to us on our own turns;
- our own digs.

The candidate set was worked out by intersecting the noisy distance bounds from those published readings. By the end, F8, G8, and F9 were the only squares consistent with every shared reading, so the crew split those three. I was closest to F8, dug it on my turn, and it was the cave. Nothing from the game’s internal state or any non-player tool was used.
